# Current Execution Context Example

Copy this file to `.agent/current_execution_context.md` only for local runs.
The live file is ignored and must not be committed.

When a new package starts, refresh the live file so the active package and
active unit match the current approved work. Stale active-package references
are a stop condition.

## Active package

Package 11 - Final public polish and closeout

## Active goal

Make the finished public repo easy to understand, run, inspect, and close out as
a portfolio asset after Package 10 is complete.

Package 11 is docs-only final polish. It clarifies the README, demo walkthrough,
package flow, output inspection guidance, public-safety stance, and closeout
checklist. It does not add new product behavior.

## Primary sources of truth

- `README.md`
- `docs/demo_walkthrough.md`
- `docs/project_closeout.md`
- `docs/packages.md`
- `docs/decisions.md`

Package 10's locked policy contract still lives in `docs/gtm_policy.md` and
must remain unchanged.

## Current unit

Package 11A - Docs-only public polish and closeout

## Default warehouse path

`data/warehouse/account_health.duckdb`

## Package 11 exclusions

Do not add:

- Model training, retraining, re-evaluation, champion selection, promotion, or
  rescoring
- New observability logic
- Changes to `gtm_policy_v1`
- New health-band or action-policy logic
- Dashboards
- Streamlit
- Frontend work
- APIs
- Cloud deployment
- CRM integrations
- Campaign execution
- Claims that synthetic-data actions are commercially validated
- Screenshots pretending to be a real production UI
- Generated or local-only artefacts in git

## Package 11 stop conditions

Stop before:

- Starting Package 11 if Package 10 is not committed
- Changing `gtm_policy_v1` thresholds, taxonomy, or boundary behaviour without
  an explicit durable-doc decision/update
- Adding new code or product behavior rather than documentation closeout work
- Using real customer or company data
- Adding dashboards, APIs, cloud services, CRM integration, or campaign
  execution
- Claiming real commercial validation from synthetic outputs
- Weakening tests or public repo safety
- Committing generated, local-only, private, or environment-specific files

## Security reminders

Do not commit:

- `AGENTS.override.md`
- `.agent/current_execution_context.md`
- `.agent/package_gate.md`
- `.agent/agent_runbook.md`
- `.env`
- `.pytest_cache/`
- `scripts/__pycache__/`
- `tests/__pycache__/`
- `src/**/__pycache__/`
- `mlruns/`
- `*.duckdb`
- `*.duckdb.wal`
- `*.db`
- `data/generated/`
- `data/warehouse/`
- `data/processed/`
- `data/outputs/`
- `artifacts/models/`
- `artifacts/tmp/`
- `*.egg-info/`
